<title>NETHERLANDS: Hoogovens says H1 aluminium demand rose.</title>
<headline>Hoogovens says H1 aluminium demand rose.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERWIJK, Netherlands 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Demand for aluminium products improved in the first half of the year, Dutch aluminium and steel group Hoogovens said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Announcing half year results, Hoogovens said higher demand helped Hoogovens' aluminium division to lift pre-tax profits of 38 million guilders against 25 million in the 1996 period.</p>
<p>Prices of primary metal recovered to reach around the same level as in the first half 1996. Selling prices of rolled and extruded products also recovered but were below those of a year earlier with a consequent squeeze on margins, the company said.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
